ed revision reviewed an entry — and gated it at membership anyway. Documenting an open bound is not closing it, which is why the fix is a derivation rather than a stricter string.\n\n## What r12 does\n\nNew rule **X1-P** derives the revision each register entry first entered the contract in, from evidence *older than the claim*:\n\n- **snapshot-proven** — the digest-pinned per-revision baselines the preservation harnesses already consume. `X1-C1` is absent from `r8`/`r9`, present in `r10`, so the answer is computed from files no edit to the contract can reach.\n- **summary-attested** — fallback for an entry older than the oldest baseline (`X1-A1` → `r3`), **refused** wherever the chain can decide.\n- both cross-checked against a new `revisionLog[].introduces` record.\n\nThe chain is protected against *narrowing* as well as tampering, and `known-revision` is removed from the implemented vocabulary so r11's bound can't return as a declaration.\n\n**Beyond the ask, one thing:** the same class was in the ACTIVE register, unreported by any verdict and strictly worse — `reviewedIn` there was required only to be non-empty, so it accepted `2026-07-28.r99`. That register's entry authorises the Sparkle exception that *is* in the shipped macOS host bundle. Both registers are gated now, each under the rule that owns it (R26 / R39), so verdict 10's own control fails under the rule it named.\n\nThe independent `reviewer-gates.sh` had been checking the same insufficient predicate — verdict 10's control passed there too. Rewritten to load the chain from disk and derive the introduction itself.\n\n## Gates — real exit codes, in place from the resource layout\n\nvalidator 2862 checks · mutations **285/285** (four corrupt a *baseline*, not a claim about one) · board consumers · preservation 122/201/143/**245** · reviewer-gates with 8 negative controls · legacy guard · `task-board validate` — all **exit 0**.\n\n## Two things reported, not smoothed over\n\n- **`swift test` flakes on this tree, unrelated to r12**: 3 failures in 24 full runs, all `snapshot.activeConnections → 1) == 0` in `HEVUDPDatagramAdapterTests:646` and `:333`. `git status` over `Sources`/`Tests`/manifests/`.spec` was empty the whole session. Both assertions read `await adapter.snapshot()` right after `receiveEOF` while the adapter decrements the counter in its own task. Raised as **BUG-260728-2j25tu**, not fixed from a decision-artifact task.\n- `TASK-260728-q5kjta`'s scope re-pointed `r11 → r12` (rule A1); the revision label was the only edit.","ttft_ms":3572,"ttft_stream_ms":2981,"time_to_request_ms":61,"type":"result","duration_ms":2575634,"uuid":"1688a98f-6d16-4f12-a0de-242d504c861d"}
